---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
// import Link from "../../components/Link.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import complex_starter from "../../img/p5/complex-starter.png"
import attractor from "../../img/p5/attractor.png"
import secret from "../../img/iu000170_fmc/secret.png"
---
<Slide t2="Complex Iteration">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">We can build geometric patterns through repeated
            multiplication in the complex plane
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="fragment flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ complex_starter }
            alt="Complex Starter"
            height="375"
            width="375" />
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">Experiment with different multiplier values</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Attractors">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">
            Let's build an interactive version of this
        </li>

        <li class="fragment">
            We are going to use an equation of the form \( c = c * c + s \)
            (where \( s \) means "shift")
        </li>

        <div class="fragment flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ attractor }
                alt="Attractor"
                height="375"
                width="375" />
        </div>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Exploring Attractors">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">
            These attractor values either converge or escape
        </li>

        <li class="fragment">
            Let's plot a 2D grid of values (\(-2\) to \(2\), \(-2i\) to \(2i\))
            to see which
            ones are convergent or divergent
        </li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide>
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="javascript" lines="*|2-5|10-17|19-23" height="500px">
            { `
        for (let x of math.range(0, 100).toArray()) {
            for (let y of math.range(0, 100).toArray()) {
                let re = map(x, 0, 99, -2, 2)
                let im = map(y, 0, 99, -2, 2)
                let c = math.complex(re, im)

                // We count iterations:
                let iteration = 0

                // Starting position:
                let position = math.complex(0, 0)

                // Iterate, exit if we leave the canvas:
                while (iteration < 50 && position.abs(position) < 2) {
                    position = math.chain(position).multiply(position).add(c).done()
                    iteration++
                }

                if (iteration == 50) {
                    fill(0)
                } else {
                    fill(255)
                }
                ...
            }
        }
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Final Appearance">
    <div class="fragment flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ secret }
            alt="Secret"
            height="400"
            width="400" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Enhancements">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">
            How might we go about adding greyscale or colour?
        </li>

        <li class="fragment">
            (For points that escape, we can map the number of
            iterations to a colour value)
        </li>

        <li class="fragment">
            How might we <em>zoom in</em> to the visual form?
        </li>
    </ul>
</Slide>